@prefix geometry: <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#> .
@prefix interface: <urn:silmaril:user:interface:> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix portal: <urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:> .
@prefix projection: <urn:silmaril:user:interface:projection:> .
@prefix schema1: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

portal:ArchitecturePage a portal:Artifact ;
    portal:content """---
permalink: /architecture/
layout: default
title: "Architecture | Silmaril"
description: "The unary byte-frame law in brief — T -> Frame(X, Y) — and the implementation obligations that remain open."
---

<header class="page-hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">The Unary Byte-Frame Law</p>
    <h1>Architecture</h1>
    <p class="hero-subtitle">
        One law governs every callable in this repository: one explicit input, one
        explicit physical frame result. The repository declares a typed arrow architecture. Its current tooling
        still has migration gaps: the renderer is not admitted, and the physical
        carrier types, dependency effects, and unary launcher remain incomplete.
    </p>
</header>

{% include build-status.html %}

<section id="law" class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-container">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">The law in brief</p>
        <h2>One Input, One Frame</h2>

        <div class="law-display" data-mathematics="display">f:T\\longrightarrow\\operatorname{Frame}(X,Y)</div>

        <p>
            Every exposed callable — independent of language, file type, path, or
            generated status — must be inventoried as a typed arrow with one explicit input
            and one explicit physical frame result. The frame is a typed product, not a
            tuple, <code>Either</code>, <code>Try</code>, or implicit exception: input,
            output, and error-or-effect are separately navigable coordinates.
        </p>
        <ul class="doc-links">
            <li><strong>Active-red honesty.</strong> The law's status is
                <em>active red migration</em>: it is specified in full while the enforcement
                implementation does not yet satisfy the law it enforces. Provisional and gap
                rows are recorded over pretense — a bounded census cannot be green while a
                shortcut remains.</li>
            <li><strong>Full lexical identity.</strong> No abbreviation, acronym, or fused
                expansion is an internal coordinate. Internally it is
                <code>shapes/constraint/language</code>, <code>query/protocol/language</code>,
                <code>resource/description/framework</code> — spellings like
                <code>SHACL</code>, <code>SPARQL</code>, <code>gpg</code> survive only as
                immutable external evidence on the far side of a registered bridge.</li>
            <li><strong>Boundary evidence.</strong> Git hooks, workflow steps, and browser
                behavior remain in scope. A boundary needs typed registration, explicit
                effects, and readback evidence; a header or import alias cannot provide admission.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The full law — semantic ancestry, build bootstrap boundary, normative boundary,
            explicit binding and observation, sealed self-hosting closure — is the
            authoritative document
            docs/unary-byte-frame-law.md (embedded below).
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="typed-tree" class="section section-alt page-section">
    <div class="section-container">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">The Python realization</p>
        <h2>Leaves, Gates, Constants, Ledgers</h2>
        <p>
            The executable tree rooted at <code>scripts/python/pylib</code> admits exactly
            three leaf filenames, each carrying one public symbol:
        </p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
            <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Leaf</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Role</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>value.py</code></td>
                        <td><code>VALUE</code></td>
                        <td>A typed value leaf. Type identity, occurrence identity, schema,
                            exact ancestry, and physical byte descent must remain distinct.
                            A raw host byte string or tuple does not establish that contract.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>library.py</code></td>
                        <td><code>DEPENDENCY</code></td>
                        <td>An explicit dependency boundary. The binding needs a typed
                            contract, effect carrier, and readback evidence. An external
                            import renamed <code>DEPENDENCY</code> is not sufficient.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>process.py</code></td>
                        <td><code>MAIN</code></td>
                        <td>A unary arrow: <code>MAIN(input: Input) -&gt; Frame</code>, with
                            one explicit typed non-default input. Importing the module
                            performs no invocation. A separately typed host-exit boundary
                            observes both frame coordinates before host termination.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <ul class="doc-links">
            <li><strong>The make envelope.</strong> Build targets compose the existing
                tools. Their process receipts are useful observations, but they do not
                substitute for typed output and effect carriers.</li>
            <li><strong>The ledgers.</strong> A declared application count does not prove
                unary behavior. The required runtime suite must check the actual
                implementation, imports, constructor behavior, and host boundary.</li>
            <li><strong>Separate gates.</strong> Foundation and folded-algebra checks,
                consolidation, provenance, runtime contracts, and browser rendering
                answer separate questions. The site admission gate currently rejects execution.</li>
        </ul>
        <pre class="command-block">export SILMARIL_PYTHON=$(command -v python3)
make -C scripts/python/pylib morphism-provenance-trust-manifest-check
make -C scripts/python/pylib morphism-provenance-commit-policy-default
make -C scripts/python/pylib morphism-ontology-consolidation-check
make -C scripts/python/pylib morphism-ontology-validation</pre>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="morphism-map" class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-container">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">The morphism family map</p>
        <h2>Two Pipelines</h2>
        <p>
            The families live under
            <code>silmaril/sparky/morphism/&hellip;</code> with mirrored constants and gates.
            The map below describes the intended process families composed by
            <code>make</code>. It does not certify their unary implementation or admission.
        </p>

        <div class="pipeline-grid">
            <div class="pipeline-card">
                <h4>provenance / trust</h4>
                <ol class="pipeline-steps">
                    <li><code>trust/manifest/extraction</code> — fingerprints, policy classes,
                        key files, identities out of the ontology turtle</li>
                    <li><code>trust/manifest/render</code> — the manifest document</li>
                    <li>drift gate &mdash; byte-compare against the committed
                        <code>keys/trust-manifest.txt</code></li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-card">
                <h4>provenance / commit</h4>
                <ol class="pipeline-steps">
                    <li><code>commit/keyring/construction</code> — ephemeral keyring from committed public keys</li>
                    <li><code>commit/observation/header</code> and
                        <code>commit/observation/verification</code> — raw commit headers and
                        <code>gpg</code> verification evidence</li>
                    <li><code>commit/classification/*</code> — <code>signature/type</code>, then
                        <code>good</code>, <code>attested</code>, <code>secure/shell</code>,
                        <code>unsigned</code>, <code>unknown</code>, <code>bad/signature</code></li>
                    <li><code>commit/record/merge</code> — one classified record per commit</li>
                    <li><code>commit/policy/{default, report, strict}</code> — the exit-status gate</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="pipeline-note">See <a href="{{ '/provenance/' | relative_url }}">Provenance</a>
                    for what the classes mean and how the server bridge uses them.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-card">
                <h4>ontology / consolidation</h4>
                <ol class="pipeline-steps">
                    <li><code>consolidation/source/discovery</code> — enumerate <code>basicttl/</code></li>
                    <li><code>consolidation/document/normalization</code> — per-document cleanup
                        (illegal local names percent-encoded)</li>
                    <li><code>consolidation/namespace/union/projection</code> — one namespace union</li>
                    <li><code>consolidation/{corpus, entity, statement}/tally</code> — census counts</li>
                    <li>five renders — <code>consolidated/render</code>,
                        <code>shapes/constraint/language/document/render</code>,
                        <code>query/protocol/language/document/emission</code>,
                        <code>geographic/query/protocol/language/document/emission</code>,
                        <code>manifest/render</code></li>
                    <li>sync gate &mdash; the five artifacts must byte-match
                        <code>ontology/</code>; regeneration is the documented copy in
                        ontology/README.md (embedded below)</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-card">
                <h4>ontology / validation</h4>
                <ol class="pipeline-steps">
                    <li><code>document/parse</code> — the consolidated graph parses</li>
                    <li><code>shapes/conformance</code> — shapes-constraint-language conformance
                        over the consolidated graph</li>
                    <li><code>queries/parse</code> — the query library parses</li>
                    <li><code>queries/execution</code> — the executable queries run and return rows</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="pipeline-note">External libraries enter only through gates:
                    <code>resource_description_framework_library</code> and
                    <code>shapes_constraint_language_library</code>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Further reading</h3>
        <ul class="doc-links">
            <li>The Universal Unary Byte-Frame Law (embedded below) — the authoritative law, amendments, and red receipts.</li>
            <li>Der Pr&auml;riehund und die Demokratie der Kategorien (embedded below) — why the repository prefers a provisional frame to a false taxon.</li>
            <li><a href="{{ '/provenance/' | relative_url }}">Provenance</a> — the trust system this machinery enforces.</li>
            <li><a href="{{ '/folklore/' | relative_url }}">Folklore</a> — the same architecture, as story and as ontology.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

{% include documentation.html source="docs/praeriehund-demokratie-der-kategorien.md" %}

{% include documentation.html source="docs/unary-byte-frame-law.md" %}

{% include documentation.html source="ontology/README.md" %}
""" ;
    portal:path "docs/architecture.html" .

portal:Artifacts portal:query """PREFIX portal: <urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:>
SELECT ?path ?root ?content WHERE { ?artifact a portal:Artifact ; portal:path ?path . OPTIONAL { ?artifact portal:root ?root } OPTIONAL { ?artifact portal:content ?content } } ORDER BY ?path""" .

portal:BrowserBehavior a portal:Artifact,
        portal:BrowserModule ;
    portal:content """/* Browser mechanics for ontology-owned presentation and repository observations. */
(() => {
  'use strict';
  const base = document.body.dataset.basePath || '';
  const local = path => base + path;
  const make = (tag, text, attributes = {}) => {
    const node = document.createElement(tag);
    if (text !== undefined) node.textContent = text;
    Object.entries(attributes).forEach(([name, value]) => node.setAttribute(name, value));
    return node;
  };
  const button = (text, action) => {
    const node = make('button', text, {type: 'button'});
    node.addEventListener('click', action);
    return node;
  };
  const unfold = target => {
    for (let node = target; node; node = node.parentElement) if (node.tagName === 'DETAILS') node.open = true;
  };
  const revealHash = () => {
    if (!location.hash) return;
    let identifier;
    try { identifier = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1)); } catch { return; }
    const target = document.getElementById(identifier);
    if (target) { unfold(target); target.scrollIntoView({block: 'start'}); }
  };
  window.addEventListener('hashchange', revealHash);

  // Closed shelves do not fetch frame documents until a reader opens them.
  const shelves = [...document.querySelectorAll('.embedded-document')];
  shelves.forEach(shelf => shelf.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
    const frame = shelf.querySelector('iframe[data-src]');
    if (shelf.open && frame && !frame.hasAttribute('src')) frame.src = frame.dataset.src;
  }));
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-shelf]').forEach(control => control.addEventListener('click', () => shelves.filter(shelf => !shelf.hidden).forEach(shelf => { shelf.open = control.dataset.shelf === 'open'; })));
  const documentSearch = document.getElementById('document-search');
  const filterDocuments = () => {
    const text = (documentSearch?.value || '').toLowerCase();
    shelves.forEach(shelf => { shelf.hidden = !shelf.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(text); });
    const count = document.getElementById('document-count');
    if (count) count.textContent = `${shelves.filter(shelf => !shelf.hidden).length} / ${shelves.length}`;
  };
  documentSearch?.addEventListener('input', filterDocuments);
  filterDocuments();

  // Native disclosure elements preserve keyboard operation and heading targets.
  const documentContent = document.getElementById('document-content');
  if (documentContent) {
    const contents = document.getElementById('document-toc');
    const used = new Set();
    let outline = [];
    documentContent.querySelectorAll('h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6').forEach((heading, index) => {
      let identifier = heading.id || heading.textContent.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}]+/gu, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '') || `section-${index}`;
      if (used.has(identifier)) identifier += `-${index}`;
      used.add(identifier); heading.id = identifier;
      const item = make('li'); item.dataset.level = heading.tagName;
      const level = Number(heading.tagName.slice(1));
      outline = outline.filter(entry => entry.level < level);
      const parent = outline.at(-1);
      if (parent && !parent.children) { parent.children = make('ol'); parent.item.append(parent.children); }
      item.append(make('a', heading.textContent, {href: '#' + encodeURIComponent(identifier)}));
      (parent ? parent.children : contents).append(item);
      outline.push({level, item});
    });
    let sections = [];
    [...documentContent.childNodes].forEach(node => {
      if (node.nodeType === 1 && /^H[1-6]$/.test(node.tagName)) {
        const level = Number(node.tagName.slice(1));
        sections = sections.filter(entry => entry.level < level);
        if (level === 1) return;
        const disclosure = make('details', undefined, {class: 'document-chapter'}); disclosure.open = true;
        disclosure.dataset.level = node.tagName;
        const parent = sections.at(-1)?.disclosure;
        if (parent) parent.append(disclosure); else node.before(disclosure);
        const summary = make('summary'); summary.append(node); disclosure.append(summary);
        sections.push({level, disclosure});
      } else if (sections.length) sections.at(-1).disclosure.append(node);
    });
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-fold]').forEach(control => control.addEventListener('click', () => documentContent.querySelectorAll('details').forEach(section => { section.open = control.dataset.fold === 'open'; })));
    contents.addEventListener('click', event => {
      const anchor = event.target.closest('a[href^="#"]');
      const target = anchor && document.getElementById(decodeURIComponent(anchor.hash.slice(1)));
      if (target) { unfold(target); target.scrollIntoView({block: 'start'}); }
    });
    // Keep links between repository Markdown documents inside the reading surface.
    fetch(local('/assets/data/documents.json')).then(response => response.json()).then(documents => {
      const paths = new Map(documents.map(item => [item.source, item.identity]));
      documentContent.querySelectorAll('a[href]').forEach(anchor => {
        const href = anchor.getAttribute('href');
        if (!href || /^(#|https?:|mailto:)/.test(href)) return;
        const resolved = new URL(href, 'https://repository.invalid/' + document.body.dataset.source);
        const source = decodeURIComponent(resolved.pathname.slice(1));
        if (paths.has(source)) anchor.href = local('/documents/' + paths.get(source) + '/') + resolved.hash;
        else if (source.startsWith('basicttl/') && source.endsWith('.ttl')) { anchor.href = local('/explore/?file=') + encodeURIComponent(source); anchor.target = '_top'; }
      });
    }).catch(() => { documentContent.dataset.links = 'unavailable'; });
  }

  // Math is rendered locally; text alternatives remain in KaTeX's MathML output.
  if (window.katex) {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-mathematics], script[type^="math/tex"]').forEach(source => {
      const target = source.tagName === 'SCRIPT' ? make('span', undefined, {class: 'mathematical-expression'}) : source;
      const expression = source.textContent;
      if (target !== source) source.replaceWith(target);
      window.katex.render(expression, target, {displayMode: source.dataset.mathematics === 'display' || (source.type || '').includes('display'), throwOnError: false, trust: false, output: 'htmlAndMathml'});
    });
    if (window.renderMathInElement) window.renderMathInElement(document.body, {throwOnError: false, trust: false, delimiters: [{left:'$$',right:'$$',display:true},{left:'\\\\[',right:'\\\\]',display:true},{left:'\\\\(',right:'\\\\)',display:false}]});
  }
  revealHash();

  const workbench = document.getElementById('ontology-workbench');
  if (!workbench) return;
  const status = document.getElementById('catalog-status');
  const navigation = document.getElementById('ontology-tree');
  const inspector = document.getElementById('ontology-inspector');
  const search = document.getElementById('ontology-search');
  const kind = document.getElementById('ontology-kind');
  let catalog, labels, files, entities, sequence = 0;
  const cache = new Map();
  const short = value => value.split(/[#/:]/).filter(Boolean).pop() || value;
  const read = async url => { const response = await fetch(url); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(response.status + ' ' + url); return response.json(); };
  const fileData = key => {
    if (!cache.has(key)) cache.set(key, read(local('/assets/data/ontology/' + key + '.json')).catch(error => { cache.delete(key); throw error; }));
    return cache.get(key);
  };
  const disclosure = (title, content, open = false) => { const node = make('details', undefined, {class: 'inspector-panel'}); node.open = open; node.append(make('summary', title), content); return node; };
  const fail = error => { inspector.replaceChildren(make('h2', labels.error), make('p', error.message)); };
  const termControl = value => {
    if (value.kind === 'literal') {
      const node = make('span', value.value, {class: 'literal-value'});
      if (value.language || value.datatype) node.append(make('small', value.language ? '@' + value.language : '^^' + value.datatype));
      return node;
    }
    const node = button(entities.get(value.value)?.label || short(value.value), () => inspectEntity(value.value));
    node.className = 'term-link'; node.title = value.value; return node;
  };
  const tripleTable = triples => {
    const wrapper = make('div', undefined, {class:'statement-list'});
    let limit = 0;
    const more = button(labels.more, append);
    function append() {
      const next = triples.slice(limit, limit + 100); limit += next.length;
      next.forEach(triple => { const row = make('div', undefined, {class:'statement'}); triple.forEach(term => { const cell = make('div'); cell.append(termControl(term)); row.append(cell); }); wrapper.insertBefore(row, more); });
      more.hidden = limit >= triples.length;
    }
    wrapper.append(more); append(); return wrapper;
  };
  const sourcePanel = data => {
    const box = make('div');
    if (data.context.length) box.append(make('p', labels.context), make('pre', data.context.map(([prefix, namespace]) => prefix + ': ' + namespace).join('\\n')));
    if (data.error) box.append(make('p', labels.parse, {class:'parse-error'}), make('pre', data.error));
    box.append(make('pre', data.source, {class:'turtle-source'}));
    return disclosure(labels.source + ' · ' + data.path, box, Boolean(data.error));
  };
  const updateAddress = selection => {
    const url = new URL(location); url.search = ''; Object.entries(selection).forEach(([key,value]) => url.searchParams.set(key,value)); history.pushState(selection,'',url);
  };
  async function inspectFile(key, address = true) {
    const ticket = ++sequence;
    try {
      const data = await fileData(key); if (ticket !== sequence) return;
      if (address) updateAddress({file:data.path});
      inspector.replaceChildren(make('h2', data.path), make('p', `${data.triples.length} ${labels.triples.toLowerCase()}`), make('p', data.digest, {class:'source-digest'}));
      inspector.append(disclosure(labels.triples, tripleTable(data.triples), true), sourcePanel(data));
      inspector.dataset.selection = data.path;
    } catch (error) { if(ticket === sequence) fail(error); }
  }
  function relationshipList(title, identifiers) {
    const list = make('ul');
    identifiers.forEach(identifier => { const item = make('li'); item.append(termControl({kind:'iri',value:identifier})); list.append(item); });
    if (!identifiers.length) list.append(make('li',labels.none));
    return disclosure(title, list, true);
  }
  function neighborhood(entry, children) {
    const namespace = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    const vector = (tag, attributes, text) => { const node = document.createElementNS(namespace,tag); Object.entries(attributes).forEach(([key,value]) => node.setAttribute(key,value)); if(text) node.textContent=text; return node; };
    const diagram = vector('svg',{viewBox:'0 0 620 220',role:'img','aria-label':labels.diagram,class:'neighborhood-diagram'});
    const rows = [entry.parents.slice(0,3),[entry.iri],children.slice(0,3)];
    rows.forEach((identifiers,row) => identifiers.forEach((identifier,index) => {
      const horizontal = (index+1)*620/(identifiers.length+1), vertical = 35+row*75;
      if(row!==1) diagram.append(vector('line',{x1:horizontal,y1:vertical,x2:310,y2:110,stroke:'#528267','stroke-width':'2'}));
      diagram.append(vector('circle',{cx:horizontal,cy:vertical,r:'9',fill:'#205943'}));
      const title=entities.get(identifier)?.label||short(identifier);
      const text=vector('text',{x:horizontal,y:vertical+24,'text-anchor':'middle',fill:'#17372b'},title.length>27?title.slice(0,24)+'…':title);diagram.append(text);
    }));
    const viewport = make('div', undefined, {class:'diagram-viewport',tabindex:'0',role:'region','aria-label':labels.diagram});
    viewport.append(diagram, make('p', labels.diagramScope));
    return viewport;
  }
  async function inspectEntity(identifier, address = true) {
    const ticket = ++sequence;
    try {
      const entry = entities.get(identifier);
      if(address) updateAddress({entity:identifier});
      inspector.replaceChildren(make('h2',entry?.label||short(identifier)),make('code',identifier,{class:'entity-identity'}));
      inspector.dataset.selection=identifier;
      if(!entry){inspector.append(make('p',labels.unindexed));return;}
      const sources = await Promise.all(entry.files.map(fileData)); if(ticket!==sequence)return;
      const children = catalog.entities.filter(value=>value.parents.includes(identifier)).map(value=>value.iri);
      const copy=button(labels.copy,async()=>{try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(identifier);copy.textContent=labels.copied;}catch{copy.textContent=identifier;}}); inspector.append(copy);
      if(entry.kind==='class') inspector.append(neighborhood(entry,children),relationshipList(labels.parents,entry.parents),relationshipList(labels.children,children));
      inspector.append(relationshipList(labels.types,entry.types));
      sources.forEach(data=>{
        const section=make('section'); section.append(make('h3',data.path),disclosure(labels.outgoing,tripleTable(data.triples.filter(row=>row[0].value===identifier)),true),disclosure(labels.incoming,tripleTable(data.triples.filter(row=>row[2].kind!=='literal'&&row[2].value===identifier))),sourcePanel(data));inspector.append(section);
      });
    } catch(error){if(ticket===sequence)fail(error);}
  }
  const trie = {directories:new Map(),files:[]};
  function directoryContent(branch) {
    const list=make('ul');
    [...branch.directories.entries()].sort(([a],[b])=>a.localeCompare(b)).forEach(([name,child])=>{
      const item=make('li'),folder=make('details'),summary=make('summary',name);folder.append(summary);
      folder.addEventListener('toggle',()=>{if(folder.open&&!folder.dataset.loaded){folder.dataset.loaded='true';folder.append(directoryContent(child));}});
      item.append(folder);list.append(item);
    });
    branch.files.forEach(file=>{const item=make('li'),control=button(file.path.split('/').pop()+(file.error?' ⚠':''),()=>inspectFile(file.key));control.title=file.path;item.append(control);list.append(item);});
    return list;
  }
  function results() {
    const needle=search.value.toLowerCase().trim();navigation.replaceChildren();
    if(kind.value==='files'&&!needle){navigation.append(directoryContent(trie));return;}
    const matches=kind.value==='files'?catalog.files.filter(file=>file.path.toLowerCase().includes(needle)):catalog.entities.filter(entry=>entry.kind===kind.value&&(entry.label.toLowerCase().includes(needle)||entry.iri.toLowerCase().includes(needle)));
    navigation.append(make('p',String(matches.length),{role:'status'}));
    let offset=0;const more=button(labels.more,append);navigation.append(more);
    function append(){matches.slice(offset,offset+100).forEach(entry=>{const control=button(entry.path||entry.label,()=>entry.path?inspectFile(entry.key):inspectEntity(entry.iri));control.className='explorer-result';control.title=entry.path||entry.iri;navigation.insertBefore(control,more);});offset+=100;more.hidden=offset>=matches.length;}
    if(matches.length)append();else navigation.prepend(make('p',labels.empty));
  }
  function selectionFromAddress() {
    const parameters=new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    if(parameters.has('entity'))inspectEntity(parameters.get('entity'),false);
    else if(parameters.has('file')){const entry=catalog.files.find(file=>file.path===parameters.get('file'));if(entry)inspectFile(entry.key,false);else inspector.replaceChildren(make('p',labels.empty));}
  }
  Promise.all([read(local('/assets/data/portal.json')),read(local('/assets/data/ontology.json'))]).then(([words,data])=>{
    labels=words;catalog=data;files=new Map(data.files.map(file=>[file.key,file]));entities=new Map(data.entities.map(entry=>[entry.iri,entry]));
    catalog.files.forEach(file=>{const parts=file.path.split('/');parts.pop();let branch=trie;parts.forEach(part=>{if(!branch.directories.has(part))branch.directories.set(part,{directories:new Map(),files:[]});branch=branch.directories.get(part);});branch.files.push(file);});
    status.textContent=`${data.files.length.toLocaleString()} ${labels.fileCount} · ${data.entities.length.toLocaleString()} ${labels.entityCount} · ${data.errors} ${labels.parseCount} · ${labels.revision} ${data.revision.slice(0,8)}`;
    workbench.dataset.ready='true';results();selectionFromAddress();
    search.addEventListener('input',results);kind.addEventListener('change',results);document.getElementById('ontology-clear').addEventListener('click',()=>{search.value='';results();search.focus();});
    window.addEventListener('popstate',selectionFromAddress);
  }).catch(error=>{status.textContent=error.message;status.setAttribute('role','alert');});
})();
""" ;
    portal:path "docs/assets/js/portal.js" .

portal:Chapter a owl:Class .

portal:DefaultLayout a portal:Artifact ;
    portal:content """<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{{ page.title | default: site.title }}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page.description | default: site.description }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/main.css' | relative_url }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/generated.css' | relative_url }}">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,300;0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body class="{{ page.layout }}" data-base-path="{{ site.baseurl }}">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
    <nav class="site-nav">
        <div class="nav-container">
            <a href="{{ '/' | relative_url }}" class="site-title">Silmaril</a>
            <div class="nav-links">
                <a href="{{ '/explore/' | relative_url }}">Ontology atlas</a>
                <a href="{{ '/architecture/' | relative_url }}">Architecture</a>
                <a href="{{ '/provenance/' | relative_url }}">Provenance</a>
                <a href="{{ '/folklore/' | relative_url }}">Folklore</a>
                {% include reading-navigation.html %}
                <a href="https://github.com/groenewt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <main id="main-content">
        {{ content }}
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
        <div class="footer-container">
            <p>An open notebook for structures, strategies, and the evidence between them.</p>
            <p class="footer-meta">Tristan Groenewold / <a href="https://github.com/groenewt">github.com/groenewt</a></p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/vendor/katex/katex.min.css' | relative_url }}">
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/vendor/katex/katex.min.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/vendor/katex/contrib/auto-render.min.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/portal.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
</body>
</html>
""" ;
