<urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:element:3> a portal:Paragraph ;
    geometry:hasGeometry <urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:geometry:3> ;
    interface:text "A traveler reaches the archive with a splendid claim: “This is a group.” The tortoise asks for the carrier and the operation. Does every pair have exactly one result? Does regrouping change it? A name is the beginning of the investigation." .

<urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:element:30> a portal:PageHeading ;
    geometry:hasGeometry <urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:geometry:30> ;
    interface:text "Every claim has a story. Every law leaves a trail." .

<urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:element:31> a portal:Paragraph ;
    geometry:hasGeometry <urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:geometry:31> ;
    interface:attribute <urn:silmaril:user:interface:portal:attribute:31:class> ;
    interface:text "Start with an operation and see how much it can become. Silmaril connects algebra, category theory, and economic questions through declarations you can open, equations you can read, and evidence you can question." .

